<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47660" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tēlĕphus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> ), i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τήλεφος.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A king of Mysia</i>, <i>son of
				Hercules and the nymph Auge.</i> He was wounded before Troy by
			the spear of Achilles, but was afterwards oured by its rust, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
				112</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 171</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tr. 5,
				2, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. A. P. 96</span></i>; <i><span class="en">140</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Epod. 17,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 101</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 34,
				15, 45, § 152</span></i>; <i><span class="en">25, 5, 19, §
			42</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A contemporary and friend of Horace</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3,
				19, 26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 13, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 11,
		21</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
